\name{cellucid_history_turn_undo}
\alias{cellucid_history_turn_undo}
\title{Undo a turn}
\usage{
cellucid_history_turn_undo(viewer, turn, only_own = FALSE)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{turn}{A turn, by its id (history_summary lists them). Text (at least 1 character). Required.}
\item{only_own}{Delete only the turn's own steps, keeping the others (to Recently deleted). \code{TRUE} or \code{FALSE}. Default \code{FALSE}, the viewer's own.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome: a list of \code{head} (The step shown now), \code{journal}, \code{other_branches} (Branches holding more of its steps, undone there separately), \code{removed} (Steps deleted (only_own)).
}
\description{
Take back one agent or notebook turn on the branch shown: show the step before it, or, with only_own, delete only the turn's own steps (applying the others again) when someone else's steps came in between.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{history.turn.undo} (History). It moves the viewer's history, as the person's Undo, Redo or a click on a step does: it makes no step of the history.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_history_turn_undo(viewer, turn = "turn-1")
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
